after 9/11 Airbus introduced this new  reinforced cockpit door part of that is  a system that controls three locks  there's a code pad outside the cockpit  for crew members press a button that  notifies the pilot that you want to be  allowed in and then he uses a switch in  the cockpit to unlock the door Lufthansa  says the captain of the Germanwings  flight tried to do this of the cockpit  attempts to get back in that's one way  the system is used now a couple other  things the system can do in these are of  the most interest to investigators if a  crew member tries to enter the cockpit  then there's no response from inside  there's a four-digit code the crew  member can enter that activates a loud  buzzer and flashing light inside the  cockpit pilot doesn't do anything the  cockpit door will open automatically 30  seconds later but a pilot also has the  ability to override the code manually  and keep a door locked for up to five  minutes but thinking here is that if  there's someone who's trying to get into  that cockpit who shouldn't the pilot can  keep the intruder out
 

